# Lab 6 - Raft Election Protocol

## Usage with RPC Setup

cd into the lab6 directory

```sh
cd lab6
```

To start all your nodes simulataneously as individual processes, use the following, with <N> being the total number of nodes.

```sh
python start_election.py <N>
```

### To start the nodes individually instead:

Open up 8 terminals for the clients, you can split them with the Split Terminal button for vertical split and holding 'Alt' for horizontal splits.

In each terminal, start each node via the following command, replacing <ID> with any int within [0, N), which will create a node that listens on localhost:<8080 + ID>, where <N> is the total number of nodes for the simulation.

```sh
go run raft.go <ID> <N>
```

Try to do this somewhat quickly so that they all start around the same time.
Each process must also specify a different integer ID, such that each node has a unique ID.

### Troubleshooting

Note that if the nodes do not seem to connect to one another, try adjusting the BASE_PORT global const in BOTH `start_election.py` and `raft.go` to a different allowable port. This was found to be the cause of some issues on one our of local machines.
